[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3 uid="uid://bgubmapquarry01"]

; Twin Quarry — the sixth map, and the first built for Capture B·O·G (D-082),
; rebuilt in place against the quarry asset pack (D-140).
;
; Like Kopje Crossing, Lantern Wharf and Halcyon Wake this scene has no geometry
; in it at all. `scripts/world/maps/quarry_map.gd` extends `StaticMap` and
; builds the pit in `_ready()` from its layout tables — the floor, the rim
; cliff, the shaft with the monolith standing in it, the two cut benches with
; their walls and haul ramps, the north-west spoil bench with the adit bored
; through it, the south-east terraces, the two catwalks over the shaft, and the
; columns, berms, blocks and kerbs standing on the floor — then calls `super()`,
; which sweeps all of it into world-space trimesh collision on layer 1, and then
; adds the dressing: rubble, weeds, puddles, ramp paint, derricks, work lamps,
; the quarry asset pack and the ambience.
;
; Three things are on the solid side of that line that look like dressing, and
; each is there for one reason: **the spoil rocks and the minecarts read as
; cover, so they are cover** (the carts stand on a box built in code, not on
; the art asset's trimesh), and everything else the pack puts down — ore,
; barrels, portals, signs, rail — is obviously not cover and is walked through.
;
; The symmetry is **rotational**: Team 2's half is Team 1's half turned 180
; degrees about the origin. The two things that are not a turned pair — the
; spoil bench with the tunnel and the three terraces — both stand on the
; perpendicular bisector of the line between the bases, which is where a thing
; can be asymmetric and still be exactly as far from one base as from the other.
; See the script's header.
;
; So this file is what `static_map.gd` asks for:
;
;   Environment  hard late-morning sun, no cloud (`quarry_env.tres`). It was an
;                overcast until the rebuild; a sun-baked quarry is a shadow map.
;   Sun          50 degrees up out of the north-east, bright and white, with
;                shadows on. Serialised ROW-major, as every `.tscn` stores a
;                `Transform3D`.
;   Spawns       eight pads on the pit floor, four to a team, alternating so a
;                two-player match opens with the two players in opposite
;                corners, and every pad a rotational pair with its partner so
;                the two teams' openings are congruent. None of them is on a
;                bench: you spawn *outside* your base and run in, which is the
;                same thing an attacker has to do and is what keeps the ramps
;                the busiest ground on the map. Each faces the middle.
;   Bases        Team 1 at (-17.75, 4, -17.75), Team 2 at (17.75, 4, 17.75) —
;                the middle of each bench, four metres up, inside the wall
;                (D-051). 50.2 m apart, and neither can see the other: the
;                monolith stands in the shaft on the diagonal between them and
;                a column stands on the lip either side of it.
;   Letters      all three on the bisector, so each is exactly as far from one
;                base as from the other: G in the tunnel's corner chamber, U on
;                the shaft's south-east lip, B on the top terrace.
;
; `tools/preview_map.gd` stands a Bog on every pad, `tools/quarry_check.gd`
; measures the two flag runs against each other and proves the bases are
; congruent, `tools/parkour_report.gd` walks the jump graph, and
; `tools/playthrough.gd` plans the capture layout off the declared bases.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/world/maps/quarry_map.gd" id="1_quarry_map"]
[ext_resource type="Environment" path="res://resources/config/quarry_env.tres" id="2_quarry_env"]

